      "documentSlug": "crypto-bot-order-and-position-reconciliation",
      "documentConcept": "Crypto bot order and position reconciliation",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:9bb02c86a96dcdaefd64378d1473e92d72a8a27aa2e5037208e0d4398fba07a0",
      "text": "Order and position reconciliation compares local execution records with venue orders, fills, and exposure. The evidence distinguishes unknown request outcomes, duplicated status notifications, late fills, inconsistent adapter mappings, and snapshots that predate streamed executions. NautilusTrader documents separate order, fill, and position checks; Freqtrade documents updating exchange order state before position checks. Historical issue reports show why a monitor must preserve order identity, inspect quantities and terminal states, and qualify what a missing order or position report proves. Reconciliation labels and net position agreement alone do not establish that every execution was classified correctly.",
